.\" OpenBSD-style concise man page
.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt FREE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm free
.Nd display amount of free and used memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm free
.Op Fl bkmgh
.Op Fl t
.Op Fl w
.Op Fl s Ar N
.Op Fl c Ar N
.Op Fl Fl si
.Op Fl Fl color Ns = Ns Ar WHEN
.Op Fl Fl bar Ns = Ns Ar WHEN
.Op Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility displays the total amount of free and used physical and swap
memory on the system, as well as the buffers and cache consumed by
the kernel.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b , Fl Fl bytes
Display the amount of memory in bytes.
.It Fl k , Fl Fl kibi
Display the amount of memory in kibibytes.
This is the default.
.It Fl m , Fl Fl mebi
Display the amount of memory in mebibytes.
.It Fl g , Fl Fl gibi
Display the amount of memory in gibibytes.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl human
Show all output fields automatically scaled to the shortest
three-digit unit and display the units of print out.
Uses binary units (Ki, Mi, Gi, Ti).
.It Fl Fl si
Use powers of 1000 instead of 1024.
Modifies the behavior of
.Fl h .
.It Fl t , Fl Fl total
Display a line showing the column totals.
.It Fl w , Fl Fl wide
Switch to the wide mode.
The wide mode produces lines longer than 80 characters, splitting
.Cm buff/cache
into separate
.Cm buffers
and
.Cm cache
columns.
.It Fl Fl color Ns = Ns Ar WHEN
Color the used column by usage percent: green below 70, yellow
below 90, red otherwise.
.Ar WHEN
is
.Cm always ,
.Cm auto
(the default), or
.Cm never .
.Ev NO_COLOR
and
.Ev TERM Ns = Ns Cm dumb
disable color even with
.Cm always .
.It Fl Fl bar Ns = Ns Ar WHEN
Draw a 10-cell usage bar after each Mem and Swap row.
.Ar WHEN
is
.Cm always ,
.Cm auto
(the default), or
.Cm never .
.Cm auto
follows TTY/icon detection.
.It Fl s Ar N , Fl Fl seconds Ns = Ns Ar N
Continuously display the result every
.Ar N
seconds.
.It Fl c Ar N , Fl Fl count Ns = Ns Ar N
Repeat printing
.Ar N
times, then exit.
Without
.Fl s
the interval is one second.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.It Fl Fl help
Display a help message and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std free
.Sh EXAMPLES
Display memory usage in the default kibibyte units:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ free
               total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available
Mem:        16384000     8192000     4096000      512000     4096000    12288000
Swap:        2048000      128000     1920000
.Ed
.Pp
Display memory usage in human-readable format:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ free -h
               total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available
Mem:            16Gi         8Gi         4Gi       512Mi         4Gi        12Gi
Swap:            2Gi       128Mi         1Gi
.Ed
.Pp
Display memory with totals in mebibytes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ free -m -t
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr top 1 ,
.Xr vm_stat 1 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is not specified by POSIX.
It originated in Linux procps and is widely used on Unix-like systems.
The behavior is compatible with procps-ng
.Nm .
